6. Understand SQLAlchemy ORM
ORM stands for Object Relational Mapper.
It allows you to work with database tables using Python classes instead of writing SQL manually for every operation.
For example, instead of manually executing:
</>SQL
INSERT INTO ai_requests (model, prompt)
VALUES ('gpt-4o', 'Explain AI');
You can write Python:

new_request = AIRequestRecord(
    model="gpt-4o",
    prompt="Explain AI"
)

</>python
new_request = AIRequestRecord(
    model="gpt-4o",
    prompt="Explain AI"
)
db.add(new_request)
db.commit()

SQLAlchemy translates these Python operations into SQL.
Important distinction:
•	PostgreSQL is the database that stores your data.
•	SQLAlchemy is the Python ORM that communicates with it.
•	Psycopg is the driver that connects Python to PostgreSQL.
