File: config/database.py
</>Python
import os

from dotenv import load_dotenv

from sqlalchemy import create_engine
from sqlalchemy.orm import declarative_base, sessionmaker


load_dotenv()

DATABASE_URL = os.getenv("DATABASE_URL")

if not DATABASE_URL:
    raise RuntimeError(
        "DATABASE_URL is missing. Check your .env file."
    )


engine = create_engine(
    DATABASE_URL,
    pool_pre_ping=True
)


SessionLocal = sessionmaker(
    autocommit=False,
    autoflush=False,
    bind=engine
)


Base = declarative_base()


def get_db():

    db = SessionLocal()

    try:
        yield db

    finally:
        db.close()

Understand this code
•	load_dotenv() reads your .env file.
•	create_engine() creates the database engine.
•	SessionLocal creates database sessions.
•	Base is the parent class for database models.
•	get_db() provides a database session to an API endpoint and closes it afterwards.
A session is the unit of work through which your application reads and writes database records.
